& [BoundaryFormation] separates four fault origins
  + [request_fault] occurs before physical observation and is returned by request validation, not the result sum
  + [open_fault] is an actual nonzero CreateFileW error
  + [query_fault] is an actual nonzero error from one named Windows query
  + [observation_fault] is local bound, decoding, or semantic rejection after a successful query
  + [complete] is coherent supplied evidence

& [AtomicRequirementSet] is complete
  + [M2B-PFR-001] preserves corrective source, research, prior authority, proof, and review
  + [M2B-PFR-002] advances result profile to 0.2 and defines request profile 0.1
  + [M2B-PFR-003] adds a strict request with exact result profile, target, and canonical input root
  + [M2B-PFR-004] models exactly open_fault, query_fault, observation_fault, and complete results
  + [M2B-PFR-005] reserves open and query faults for nonzero OS errors
  + [M2B-PFR-006] defines exactly three local observation fault classes
  + [M2B-PFR-007] binds observation fault to exactly one of four closed query stages
  + [M2B-PFR-008] forbids error code and partial evidence in observation fault
  + [M2B-PFR-009] preserves complete evidence and exact disposition relations
  + [M2B-PFR-010] rejects legacy result profile 0.1 and unknown JSON
  + [M2B-PFR-011] proves zero runtime, Windows, unsafe, Cargo, and physical effects
  + [M2B-PFR-012] closes focused, global, evidence, rollback, support, narrative, and publication proof

